  "raw": "ima Vavi\nIn July there was confusion among the membership of the Congress of South African Trade Unions’ Central executive Committee (CEC). In separate statements by Zwelinzima Vavi, his general secretary and the CEC on a resolution on nationalization and the Eskom issue, they rejected each other. Now, in a clear indication as to where they both want things to go, in response to what comrades like Jessie Duarte, declined to disassociate themselves from, Vavi has acknowledged that no faction currently controls Cosatu.\nThe general secretary nailed down the formation of the new federation, in the video below:\nWhat we need in the task of rebuilding SA… Posted by Zwelinzima Vavi on Tuesday, January 28, 2020\nIn July there was confusion over the Eskom resolution at the Eskom elective conference, in which delegates rejected a proposal to nationalize the Eskom. Vavi's unity call made it clear that no faction",
  "serialized": "ima Vavi In July there was confusion among the membership of the Congress of South African Trade Unions’ Central executive Committee (CEC). In separate statements by Zwelinzima Vavi, his general secretary and the CEC on a resolution on nationalization and the Eskom issue, they rejected each other. Now, in a clear indication as to where they both want things to go, in response to what comrades like Jessie Duarte, declined to disassociate themselves from, Vavi has acknowledged that no faction currently controls Cosatu. The general secretary nailed down the formation of the new federation, in the video below: What we need in the task of rebuilding SA… Posted by Zwelinzima Vavi on Tuesday, January 28, 2020 In July there was confusion over the Eskom resolution at the Eskom elective conference, in which delegates rejected a proposal to nationalize the Eskom. Vavi's unity call made it clear that no faction",
